{{also|runup|run-up}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[run]] [[up]]|runs up|running up|ran up|run up}}

# {{context|cricket|lang=en}} of a [[bowler]], to run, or [[walk]] up to the [[bowling crease]] in order to [[bowl]] a [[ball]].
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To bring a [[flag]] to the top of its [[flag pole]].
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[make]] something, usually an item of clothing, very [[quickly]].
#: ''I'll '''run''' you '''up''' a skirt for tomorrow evening.''
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[accumulate]] a [[debt]].
#: ''He '''ran up''' over $5,000 in unpaid bills.''

===See also===
* [[run up against]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|cricket|lang=en}} the action of running up; the [[area]] of the [[pitch]] used by the bowler to run up, the start of which he marks with a small [[marker]]

